R-T30 R-SO24 R-SO6 R-SO10 R-T17 R-T19 R-SO15 R-SO14 R-T16 R-T6 (slices 079b, 080; it was `tc3-path-roc`), the compiler that a tool command selects when `default-roc` is not set and compilers are installed (entry `commands`). The home of `tc1-order` (4 installed compilers: A = nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029, B = nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27, C = nightly-2026-10-05-aaaaaaa, D = nightly-2026-10-01-bbbbbbb) but `config.toml` has no `default-roc` (only `[probe] timeout = 20`: a hand edit, R-SO24 case 3), and `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` is not set.
The `roc` on `PATH` (`fx/path-roc`, `fx/jobs` `version`) has the id C. Before slice 080 it was the selected compiler (rank 7). By R-SO6 and R-SO24 rank 6 gives the newest installed nightly or release, A, and rank 7 is not looked up: there is no `path_roc` call. Rank 7 is reached only when nothing is installed (`tc2-nothing`, `ti4-nothing`).
The pin of each app is `nightly-2026-10-11-1a2b3c4` (not installed, in the nightly list), a fake tty, `TALON_NOW=2026-10-15T12:00:00Z`. `fx/answers` is empty. The checks are the rows of `fx/units`: `two` fails with A only, `three` fails with A, C and D.

| Run | Words | Result | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `tool install acme/two` | One `list_dirs` of `<cache>/toolchains` (rank 6), no `path_roc`. A is selected, so the round of checks is A, B, C, D (the selected one first, as in `tc1-order`). `two` fails with A, so the build runs with B (the first that passes). `built with B`. No download, no `default-roc` write (a try is no download) | R-T30, R-SO6, R-SO24, R-T17, R-T19 |
| 2 | `tool install acme/three env:ROC_TOOLCHAIN=nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27` | `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` (rank 2) selects B: no `list_dirs` for the choice and no `path_roc` call. The round of checks is B, A, C, D (the selected one first, as in `tc1-order` run 2): `three` passes with B only, so the build runs with B | R-T30, R-SO2, R-SO7 |
| 3 | `tool install acme/dl --roc pinned` | `--roc pinned` skips the try. The pin is downloaded (the flag is the consent). `default-roc` is not set, so the install of the pin sets it under the lock of `config.toml` before the rename (R-SO24: each install sets the default when none is set, also when rank 6 gave a compiler for the run) | R-T30, R-SO24, R-SO15, R-T16, R-T6 |

The unpack of the app bundle is not part of this rule: `Fetch.unbundler` (R-FE4) takes the newest installed compiler (A) when no `default-roc` names one.

The note of rank 6 (R-SO24, manager answer Q2 of slice 080): a tool command that selects the compiler by rank 6 prints `note: default-roc is not set, so A, the newest installed compiler, is used. Run: tln setup, or tln roc default A` on stderr, one for each run (runs 1 and 3 here; run 2 has `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` and no note). The other tool cases that use rank 6 show it too.
